          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple"} triple
            of distinct points in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+line"} projective line
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            may be transformed by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+transformation"} projective transformation
            (an element of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+general+linear+group"} PGL(2,K)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = \mathbf{C}
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%B6bius+transformation"} Möbius transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PGL(2,K)
            is 3-transitive on the projective line). Therefore no projective invariant can be attached to a triple of points and if three points are the starting parameters for some problem in projective geometry we may and typically do give them fixed values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0,1,\infty
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^1(K) = P(K^2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(K^2)
            is also identified with
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\cup\{\infty\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^1(K)
            which sends three distinct points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B,C
            in a projective line to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty, 0,1
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^1(K)
            respectively.
          %p
            The
            %strong cross ratio
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ;
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B;C,D)
            is then the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            under this isomorphism. Conversely, given distinct points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B,C
            in a projective line and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\in K\cup\{\infty\}
            there is a unique point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ;
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B;C,D) = k
          %h2#when_the_projective_line_is_identified_with_
            When the projective line is identified with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^1(K)
          %p
            The unique element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PGL(2,K)
            that takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B, C)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 0, 1)
            may be described as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+linear+transformation"} fractional linear transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %mi A
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo −
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo −
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{A, B, C}: z \mapsto \frac{z - B}{z - A} \cdot \frac{C - A}{C - B}
          %p The simplest projective invariant can be attached to a quadruple of points and it is the cross ratio. It can be expressed in various ways, e.g.,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                      %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                      %mi D
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo −
                      %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo −
                      %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A,B,C,D) \coloneqq \frac{A - C}{A - D}\frac{B - D}{B - C}
          %p
            which is the value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{A, B, C}(D)
            using the fractional linear transformation above.
          %p
            If the cross ratio for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ;
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B;C,D)
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            and the order of the four points is changed than the cross ratio takes one of the following values, depending on the permutation:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mfrac
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\lambda, \frac{1}\lambda, 1-\lambda, \frac{1}{1-\lambda}, \frac{\lambda - 1}\lambda, \frac\lambda{\lambda-1}
          %h2#parametrized_lines_and_cross_ratio Parametrized lines and cross ratio
          %p
            Suppose the projective line is embedded in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^n(K)
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^n(K)
            by parametric equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi r
                  %mo +
                  %mi u
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho x_r = t a_r + u b_r, \,\,\,\,r = 0,\ldots,n
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi r
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = (a_r)_r
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi r
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = (b_r)_r
            are coordinates of two points,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is arbitrarily (by homogeneity) chosen constant and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau = t/u
            is a variable parameter determining a point. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = 0
            we get
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            respectively. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1,\tau_2,\tau_3,\tau_4
            are the parameters of 4 points than the parameter cross ratio
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 3
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 4
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{\tau_1 - \tau_3}{\tau_2 - \tau_3}\frac{\tau_1 - \tau_4}{\tau_2 - \tau_4}
          %p equals to the cross ratio of those 4 points.
          %h2#application_to_homogeneous_coordinates Application to homogeneous coordinates
          %p
            Given an abstract projective
            = succeed "-space" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(V)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+2)
            points. One chooses an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            vertices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_r
            will have the coordinates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_0,\ldots,x_n)
            all zero except
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_r = 1
            = succeed "-tuple" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i)_i
            is the image of a lifted basis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_i)_{i=1,\ldots,n+1}
            in the
            = succeed "-dim" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            not on any of the hyperplanes containing sides of the simplex, for which one postulates coordinates
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,\ldots,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_1+\ldots+e_{n+1}
            under the projection
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to P(V)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is preserved only if we change
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha e_i
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            does not depend on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            forces a unique choice of a basis in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            up to a common multiple, which then makes coordinates of all other points well defined. Now we want to see which coordinates are assigned to an arbitrary other point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P U
            intersects the hyperplane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_r = 0
            (containing the simplex face opposite to
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_r
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P U
            are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mi u
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho x_r = t x_r' + u 1
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_r')_r
            are coordinates of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = 0
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo +
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 = t x_r + u
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi r
                  %mo ;
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L_k, L_r; U, P)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\neq r
            calculates as the parameter cross ratio
          .maruku-equation
